From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: zed-patches <zed-patches@localhost>
Date: Tue, 24 Nov 2026 17:37:12 -0300
Subject: [PATCH] settings_ui: a Zeo badge marks the settings and pages Zeo
 added

Operator ask of 2026-11-23 (item 10): the settings window mixes Zed's
settings with the ones Zeo added, and nothing told them apart -- a setting
looked up in Zed's docs, or asked about upstream, might not exist there.

A setting Zeo added to one of Zed's pages now carries a "Zeo" chip beside
its title (render_settings_item_layout, by json_path): the Remote Projects
Button, the three card defaults, Ask Questions In Cards, MCP Servers Over
ACP and Zeo LSP For Agents. A page that is Zeo's alone -- Panel Button
Order here, and the jail's pages through the next patch -- carries it on its link and
beside its title in the breadcrumbs, not on every row (operator,
2026-11-24: there it would only repeat itself). The tooltip says "Added by
Zeo: Zed does not have this setting." (or "page").

Nothing in a setting says who added it, so zeo_badge.rs keeps the two lists
by hand. A patch that adds a setting to one of Zed's pages, or a page of
its own, adds it there too.

Tests: zeo_badge_tests.rs -- every badged path and page title exists in
the window (a later rename would otherwise drop the badge silently), and the
predicates mark Zeo's entries only.
---

